## Complete Instruction Set

Opcode values are shown as hex. `ss`/`dd` = addressing mode bits, `SS`/`DD` = register field, `RRRR` = register in immediate format, `C` = count/displacement field.

### Arithmetic (word)

| Mnemonic | Format | Opcode | Binary pattern | Operation |
|----------|--------|--------|----------------|-----------|
| A | 1 | A000 | `1010 ddDD DDss SSSS` | Dest ← Dest + Source |
| AB | 1 | B000 | `1011 ddDD DDss SSSS` | Byte add |
| AI | 8 | 0220 | `0000 0010 0010 RRRR` | R ← R + imm (next word) |
| S | 1 | 6000 | `0110 ddDD DDss SSSS` | Dest ← Dest − Source |
| SB | 1 | 7000 | `0111 ddDD DDss SSSS` | Byte subtract |
| INC | 6 | 0580 | `0000 0101 10ss SSSS` | R ← R + 1 |
| INCT | 6 | 05C0 | `0000 0101 11ss SSSS` | R ← R + 2 |
| DEC | 6 | 0600 | `0000 0110 00ss SSSS` | R ← R − 1 |
| DECT | 6 | 0640 | `0000 0110 01ss SSSS` | R ← R − 2 |
| NEG | 6 | 0500 | `0000 0101 00ss SSSS` | R ← −R |
| ABS | 6 | 0740 | `0000 0111 01ss SSSS` | R ← \|R\| (MSB=0 pos, MSB=1 neg) |
| INV | 6 | 0540 | `0000 0101 01ss SSSS` | R ← NOT R |
| MPY | 9 | 3800 | `0011 10DD DDss SSSS` | R0:R1 ← R × Source (32-bit product) |
| **MPYS** | 6 | 01C0 | `0000 0001 11ss SSSS` | **Signed** multiply → R0:R1 |
| DIV | 9 | 3C00 | `0011 11DD DDss SSSS` | R0:R1 ÷ Source → quotient R0, remainder R1 |
| **DIVS** | 6 | 0180 | `0000 0001 10ss SSSS` | **Signed** divide |

### Logical

| Mnemonic | Format | Opcode | Binary pattern | Operation |
|----------|--------|--------|----------------|-----------|
| SOC | 1 | E000 | `1110 ddDD DDss SSSS` | Dest ← Dest OR Source |
| SOCB | 1 | F000 | `1111 ddDD DDss SSSS` | Byte OR |
| SZC | 1 | 4000 | `0100 ddDD DDss SSSS` | Dest ← Dest AND NOT Source |
| SZCB | 1 | 5000 | `0101 ddDD DDss SSSS` | Byte AND NOT |
| XOR | 3 | 2800 | `0010 10CC CCss SSSS` | R ← R XOR Source |
| COC | 3 | 2000 | `0010 00DD DDss SSSS` | Compare ones corresponding; EQ flag |
| CZC | 3 | 2400 | `0010 01DD DDss SSSS` | Compare zeros corresponding |
| ANDI | 8 | 0240 | `0000 0010 0100 RRRR` | R ← R AND imm |
| ORI | 8 | 0260 | `0000 0010 0110 RRRR` | R ← R OR imm |
| CI | 8 | 0280 | `0000 0010 1000 RRRR` | Compare R with imm |

### Compare / move

| Mnemonic | Format | Opcode | Binary pattern | Operation |
|----------|--------|--------|----------------|-----------|
| C | 1 | 8000 | `1000 ddDD DDss SSSS` | Compare (Dest − Source, flags only) |
| CB | 1 | 9000 | `1001 ddDD DDss SSSS` | Byte compare |
| MOV | 1 | C000 | `1100 ddDD DDss SSSS` | Dest ← Source |
| MOVB | 1 | D000 | `1101 ddDD DDss SSSS` | Byte move |
| LI | 8 | 0200 | `0000 0010 0000 RRRR` | R ← immediate (next word) |
| CLR | 6 | 04C0 | `0000 0100 11ss SSSS` | R ← 0 |
| SETO | 6 | 0700 | `0000 0111 00ss SSSS` | R ← >FFFF |
| SWPB | 6 | 06C0 | `0000 0110 11ss SSSS` | Swap bytes in R |

### Branch / jump / subroutine

| Mnemonic | Format | Opcode | Binary pattern | Operation |
|----------|--------|--------|----------------|-----------|
| B | 6 | 0440 | `0000 0100 01ss SSSS` | Branch to address |
| BL | 6 | 0680 | `0000 0110 10ss SSSS` | Branch; R11 ← return PC |
| BLWP | 6 | 0400 | `0000 0100 00ss SSSS` | Branch; load WP/PC from vector; save context |
| X | 6 | 0480 | `0000 0100 10ss SSSS` | Execute instruction at source address |
| RTWP | 7 | 0380 | `0000 0011 1000 0000` | ST/PC/WP ← R15/R14/R13 |
| XOP | 9 | 2C00 | `0010 11DD DDss SSSS` | Extended op; BLWP to vector 0–15; R11 ← source |

**Conditional jumps** (Format 2, relative offset in low byte, −128..+127 words):

| Mnemonic | Opcode | Condition |
|----------|--------|-----------|
| JMP | 1000 | Unconditional |
| JLT | 1100 | A> = 0 and EQ = 0 |
| JLE | 1200 | L> = 0 or EQ = 1 |
| JEQ | 1300 | EQ = 1 |
| JHE | 1400 | L> = 1 or EQ = 1 |
| JGT | 1500 | A> = 1 |
| JNE | 1600 | EQ = 0 |
| JNC | 1700 | C = 0 |
| JOC | 1800 | C = 1 |
| JNO | 1900 | OV = 0 |
| JL | 1A00 | L> = 0 and EQ = 0 |
| JH | 1B00 | L> = 1 and EQ = 0 |
| JOP | 1C00 | OP = 1 |
| SBO | 1D00 | Set CRU bit to 1 (unconditional) |
| SBZ | 1E00 | Set CRU bit to 0 (unconditional) |
| TB | 1F00 | Test CRU bit → EQ |

Pattern: `0001 COND CCCC CCCC` where COND selects the condition.

> **Naming:** **High/Low** (JH, JL, JHE, JLE) test **L>** (unsigned). **Greater/Less** (JGT, JLT) test **A>** (signed).

### Shift / rotate (Format 5)

| Mnemonic | Opcode | Pattern | Operation |
|----------|--------|---------|-----------|
| SRA | 0800 | `0000 1000 CCCC SSSS` | Arithmetic shift right C places |
| SRL | 0900 | `0000 1001 CCCC SSSS` | Logical shift right |
| SLA | 0A00 | `0000 1010 CCCC SSSS` | Shift left arithmetic |
| SRC | 0B00 | `0000 1011 CCCC SSSS` | Circular shift |

- If `C = 0`, count is taken from **R0** bits 12–15 (0 → 16 shifts).
- Execution time: **12 + 2×count** cycles (+20 if count from R0).

### CRU (Communications Register Unit)

CRU is a 4096-bit I/O space addressed via **R12**.

| Mnemonic | Format | Opcode | Binary pattern | Operation |
|----------|--------|--------|----------------|-----------|
| LDCR | 4 | 3000 | `0011 00CC CCss SSSS` | Load CRU → R (1–16 bits, count in instruction) |
| STCR | 4 | 3400 | `0011 01CC CCss SSSS` | Store R → CRU (1–16 bits) |
| SBO | 2 | 1D00 | `0001 1101 CCCC CCCC` | Set CRU bit to 1 |
| SBZ | 2 | 1E00 | `0001 1110 CCCC CCCC` | Set CRU bit to 0 |
| TB | 2 | 1F00 | `0001 1111 CCCC CCCC` | Test CRU bit → EQ |

LDCR/STCR timing: **20 + 2×bits** cycles (+ CRU access overhead).

### Workspace / status control (Format 8)

| Mnemonic | Format | Opcode | Binary pattern | Operation |
|----------|--------|--------|----------------|-----------|
| LWPI | 8 | 02E0 | `0000 0010 1110 0000` | WP ← immediate (next word) |
| LIMI | 8 | 0300 | `0000 0011 0000 0000` | ST(12:15) ← immediate |
| LI | 8 | 0200 | `0000 0010 0000 RRRR` | R ← immediate |
| STWP | 8 | 02A0 | `0000 0010 1010 RRRR` | R ← WP |
| STST | 8 | 02C0 | `0000 0010 1100 RRRR` | R ← ST |
| **LST** | 8 | 0080 | `0000 0000 1000 RRRR` | **ST ← R** (TMS9995+) |
| **LWP** | 8 | 0090 | `0000 0000 1001 RRRR` | **WP ← R** (TMS9995+) |

### External instructions (Format 7)

These drive A0–A2 address lines during CRUCLK. **Not decoded on TI-99/4A** (may conflict with CRU).

| Mnemonic | Opcode | A0 A1 A2 | Notes |
|----------|--------|----------|-------|
| IDLE | 0340 | L H L | Wait for interrupt / RESET* / LOAD* |
| RSET | 0360 | L H H | Also clears interrupt mask (like LIMI 0) |
| CKON | 03A0 | H L H | Clock on (990 system) |
| CKOF | 03C0 | H H L | Clock off |
| LREX | 03E0 | H H H | Load and restart execution |

